id: pm-slack-e78x
title: "slack notify, slack test, and slack digest fail to register on pm-cli 2026.7.27 because they redeclare the host-owned --json global"
description: "pm-cli 2026.7.27 (GH-719) makes the host reject any extension command whose flags shadow a host-owned global. slack notify, slack test, and slack digest each declared { long: \"--json\" }, so registerCommand threw and all three commands failed to register against a real host. The suite never caught it because every smoke test asserted against a hand-rolled api double that accepts all registrations unconditionally. Fix: drop the flag declarations, read ctx.global.json, and rebuild the smoke suite on the SDK createExtensionTestHarness so pm's real activation engine validates registration."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-27T04:55:32.943Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T11:14:22.305Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T11:14:22.304Z"
author: pi-agent
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T04:55:42.429Z",pi-agent,"Verified end-to-end: createExtensionTestHarness activation reports failed=[] (all three commands register); npm test 66/66 green; npm run release:check green. Also fixed audit:prod script (was missing env -u npm_config_allow_scripts and --ignore-scripts, causing EALLOWSCRIPTS in the container env)."
close_reason: "Shipped and verified functionally 2026-07-28: the package installs and loads on pm-cli 2026.7.28 with failed:[] in pm health, and its commands register and execute. Closing the registration tracker."
body: ""
